# Files that two concurrent PRs commonly both append to.
# `merge=union` tells git to keep BOTH sides on conflict instead of marking
# the file as conflicted. Combined with the append-only convention in
# CAPABILITIES.md, this means concurrent PRs that each add new rows will
# merge cleanly into a file containing both new rows — no manual conflict
# resolution required.
#
# Use this driver only for files where line order is not semantically
# significant beyond chronology (changelogs, capability tables, finding
# inventories). Do NOT add code files here — union-merging Python or Go
# silently produces broken syntax.
CAPABILITIES.md merge=union

# Driver+Reviewer evidence journals are append-only by definition.
.test-evidence/*.md merge=union
